   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to permitting the Village of Upper Nyack to file an\napplication for a real property tax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S5634",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5634-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5634\n\nSPONSOR: CARLUCCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to permitting the Village of Upper\nNyack to file an application for a real property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would allow the Village of Upper Nyack to file an application\nfor exemption from real property taxes for property located in the town\nof Clarkstown, Rockland County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill authorizes the assessor of the Town of Clarks-\ntown, Rockland County, to accept an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes pursuant to section 406 of the real property tax law for\nthe 2017 and 2018 assessment roll for a parcel located at 626 North\nBroadway, in the Village of Upper Nyack within the town of Clarkstown.\n\nSection two of the bill relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would allow for a retroactive real property tax exemption for\na parcel owned by Village of Upper Nyack.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
